# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.
#
# Smolen. With five cards in one major, four in the other and game values,
# responder bids Stayman (stayman.bid gives 5-4 hands priority for it);
# when opener denies a major, responder bids three of the FOUR-card major,
# showing five of the other. Opener, who has two or three of that suit,
# bids 3NT or game in the 5-3 fit, so the notrump opener declares either
# way. With three spades and a maximum, after 3♥ opener has room to agree
# spades below game (3♠): a slam try. Once a suit is agreed the keycard
# and control-bid modules take over; nothing here names them.
#
# Written against the Stayman question, not the auction: `answered
# majors` with opener's answer denying both majors covers 1NT–2♣–2♦,
# 2NT–3♣–3♦ (Smolen_after_2N) and the same with systems on after
# interference, as BBA plays it. Notes: smolen.notes.md.

module smolen "Smolen: 5-4 in the majors after Stayman's denial"
  card   notrump.smolen.play
  needs  stayman
  param  style = general.style

when answered majors, partner.H<=3, partner.S<=3
  3H  "Smolen: four hearts, five spades, game forcing"  alert
      shows H=4, S=5, strength>=game
      when  style is not bba
      sets  forcing=game, ask=smolen(S)
      artificial
      priority 1                          # ahead of 3NT, which now denies 5-4
  3S  "Smolen: four spades, five hearts, game forcing"  alert
      shows S=4, H=5, strength>=game
      when  style is not bba
      sets  forcing=game, ask=smolen(H)
      artificial
      priority 1
  # BBA (probes/smolen-resp-1N.toml): from 10 HCP opposite 15-17, in
  # HCP; with 8-9 it bids two of the five-card major.
  3H  "Smolen: four hearts, five spades, game forcing"  alert
      shows H=4, S=5, hcp>=25-partner.hcp.min
      when  style is bba
      sets  forcing=game, ask=smolen(S)
      artificial
      priority 1
  3S  "Smolen: four spades, five hearts, game forcing"  alert
      shows S=4, H=5, hcp>=25-partner.hcp.min
      when  style is bba
      sets  forcing=game, ask=smolen(H)
      artificial
      priority 1

# Opener: two or three cards in responder's five-card major (the 2♦ or
# 3♦ answer denied four). BBA (probes/smolen-opener-3H.toml, 3S): game
# with three, 3NT with two, whatever the strength; after 3♥, 3♠ with
# three spades and a maximum (17 opposite 15-17, every time).
when asked smolen(M)
  3S    "Three spades and a maximum: slam interest"
        shows S>=3, hcp>=shown.hcp.max
        when  M is S
        sets  trump=S
        priority 1                        # ahead of 4S
  4{M}  "Three {M}: game in the five-three fit"
        shows M>=3
        sets  trump=M
  3N    "Two {M}: no fit, play 3NT"
        shows M<=2

# Responder after 3NT: no fit. The slam counts after Stayman apply
# (stayman.bid): 6NT with 32 between us, else pass.
when answered smolen(M), partner.last=3N
  6N  "No fit, but slam values"           shows points>=32-partner.hcp.min
  P   "No fit: 3NT"
      priority -5
# After a fit (4M, or opener's 3♠) the agreed suit is enough: keycard
# (rkcb-1430.bid, blackwood.bid) and control bids (control-bids.bid) read
# `we.trump` and the game force; otherwise game (base.bid).
